			],
			"Message": "fix(Wind): Use Effect.either for proper fiber-level failure handling in bootstrap\n\nReplace JavaScript try/catch with Effect.either in BootstrapImplementation to properly catch Effect failures from yield*. JavaScript try/catch cannot intercept fiber-level failures from suspended Effects - only Effect.either or Effect.catchAll can handle these.\n\nAlso simplify logsPath handling in ResolveConfiguration to use Mountain's pre-timestamped directory (e.g., .../logs/20260410T105248/window1/) directly, removing the redundant timestamp nesting that was being added client-side.\n\nThese changes ensure bootstrap stage failures are correctly captured and reported, and prevent duplicate log directory nesting.",
			"SHA": "6093daa27b6e3b9242ed2fd09713e5df29e254f7"
		}
